<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ensemble-prod.plist — launchd supervisor for the Ensemble daemon
  (Auto-Restart Phase 1, ADR-001/002/008/010/014)
  ============================================================================
  This is a REPO TEMPLATE, not an installed file. It contains literal
  INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER tokens because the plist cannot know the install
  directory at repo time. `make install` stages it with the real path
  sed'd in (INSTALL_DIR/data/ensemble-prod.plist). `make plist-install`
  copies the staged plist to ~/Library/LaunchAgents and prints the
  launchctl bootstrap command.

  DEMO USAGE (3-env topology — dev 8079 / demo 7979 / live 9797): the same
  shape works for the demo rehearsal env with three edits —
    Label              com.ensemble.demo        (must differ from prod's)
    port in your head  7979 comes from ~/agents-ensemble-demo/.env staged
                       by scripts/deploy.sh (PORT=7979) — nothing to edit
                       in the plist itself (ADR-014: env, not plist, is
                       the port source)
    INSTALL_DIR        ~/agents-ensemble-demo   (the placeholder you
                       substitute; logs land in its data/launcher.log)
  Phase 1 ships this ONE template — `make install`'s sed-in path stays
  LIVE-ONLY for now; when demo moves under launchd, duplicate this file
  with the three edits above (a make plist-demo generator is trivial but
  deferred until a launchd-managed demo is actually wanted).

  Division of labor (plan §4.1):
    launchd  = start at boot, SIGTERM stop, fixed 10s throttle, re-engage
               only if the LAUNCHER itself dies.
    launcher = exponential backoff, burst budget, exit-code mapping
               (see launcher.sh — all restart POLICY lives there, so the
               same behavior runs under systemd later).

  Health endpoints (authoritative prod port 9797, from INSTALL_DIR/.env
  staged from repo .env.prod — ADR-014/D1; plan §4.1):
    liveness : http://localhost:9797/livez
    readiness: http://localhost:9797/readyz
  launchd does NOT poll these — the launcher owns restart policy (ADR-002:
  liveness-only decisions, never readiness).

  KeepAlive semantics (ADR-010) — read before editing:
    {SuccessfulExit=false, Crashed=true} is an OR: launchd restarts the job
    when it exits nonzero (SuccessfulExit=false covers ANY nonzero exit,
    including 75 and 78) OR when it dies on a crash signal (SIGSEGV etc.).

    * Exit 0 (clean stop): NOT matched by either key → launchd stays
      hands-off. Correct: a clean stop is intentional.
    * Exit 78 (refuse — fatal config/schema): MATCHED by SuccessfulExit=
      false → launchd WILL re-run the launcher after ThrottleInterval.
      This is a real launchd limitation: KeepAlive cannot discriminate
      between exit codes. The guard is structural anyway — the launcher
      re-resolves the binary and exits 78 again without ever starting a
      child, so the "must NOT loop on 78" invariant holds at the process
      level (one no-op re-exec per ThrottleInterval, no daemon restarts).
      A `launchctl bootout` (make stop-style) keeps it down for good.
    * Exit 75 (boot tempfail): ALSO matched by SuccessfulExit=false →
      launchd would re-engage. Correct per plan: the launcher loops
      internally on 75 with its own capped backoff (ADR-011) and only
      exits after classifying a different outcome — launchd re-engaging
      happens ONLY if the launcher itself dies, which is exactly the
      belt-and-braces we want.
    * Exit 1 (burst-abort halt): matched → launchd paces re-engagement at
      ThrottleInterval. The launcher's state file re-reads the burst
      budget and re-halts if the crash pattern persists — the halt is
      therefore "stay down" from the daemon's perspective, with OS-level
      pacing providing an eventual retry probe.

  EnvironmentVariables: deliberately ABSENT. All env (PORT=9797, DB, LLM
  keys) comes from INSTALL_DIR/.env, exported by launcher.sh (ADR-014).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ensemble.prod</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/launcher.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
        <key>Crashed</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/data/launcher.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/data/launcher.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
